---
term: Self-specification burden
section: open-problems
order: 60
definition: The burden on members to state their own interests well enough for a mechanism to serve them.
seeAlso:
  - state-signal
  - stated-preference
---
Members choose what to signal and what to share, which keeps the executive from deciding what they want. People can't fully state their own interests, however. An executive that delivers exactly what a member asked for can still leave that member worse off.

A [[state signal|protected floor]] limits the harm. It doesn't remove the burden.
